# How we work (Idle Party)

Source: the owner, who vibe-codes. Last sync: **2026-11-01**.
This is the only always-on rule. `00-locks`, `10-what-to-build`,
`30-done`, `play-words`, and `hero-draw` are the full record. Open them
when their description matches. If they disagree, this page wins.

**Now:** Do the job named this turn, including the related fixes that make it true. A roadmap or week batch already taken on stays that whole batch. Do not start an unrelated feature; name it in the handoff. Commit locally when the checks are green. Cloud handoff is a branch and a PR. Do not merge, do not push a `test-*` or `v*` tag, and do not upload an AAB unless the owner asks in that turn.

## Chase

Strangers on Play become players. The party walks the room, one reason to
come back tomorrow, one Ascend loop. Principles: `docs/GROWTH_MANDATE.md`.
Do not invent a numbered program.

## Locks

Never weaken these. Dated history: `00-locks.mdc`.

| Lock | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Legal / IP | Only owned art in `assets/custom/`. No foreign dumps, sprites, or code |
| Phone | Portrait Android only. Never iOS or an Apple release. The web build is not a product |
| English UI | In-game text is English. Chat with the owner in their language |
| Fairness | Live-light DPS gate ±20% share. Trim HIGH kits. Identity can stay |
| Fight | SpatialCombat is the current sim. A second sim is allowed |
| SHOP | Gacha, BiS-for-cash, and whale packs are allowed |
| Play | Players install through Play. Do not point them at GitHub Releases |
| Upload | Never upload an AAB, push a `test-*` or `v*` tag, or start an APK workflow unless the owner asks in that turn. A source PR is not that ask |
| Cursor safety | No exploits and no foreign dumps |

## Next job

A job named this turn is the batch. Related fixes that make that job true
are part of it. A week file or year-plan slice already taken on stays the
whole batch. When this turn names no job, pick one the way
`10-what-to-build.mdc` says and build it. Do not open an unrelated feature
when the batch is green. Name that idea in the handoff.

The evidence order, grades, and “do not ask what to build” live in
`10-what-to-build.mdc`. Never invent Console percentages. Player text may
say what the code already does. Do not write a sentence the code does not
do. Write owner notes into `docs/PLAY_NOTES.md` under Open, and move them
to Done with the fix.

"Mer endgame" deepens KEY, Gauntlet, Rift, Greater Rift, and Ashen. Craft
Trial stays under MORE → CRAFT. One decision on a fork. No chairs.
`decide-a-fork.mdc` is that sentence. Do not run `/init` or clean the repo
unasked. Do not create PROJECT_INDEX, ARCHITECTURE, ROADMAP,
DEVELOPMENT_STATUS, or a second changelog.

## Done

Before you say a coding task is finished: `flutter analyze lib test --no-fatal-infos` is clean, and the matching tests in `30-done.mdc` are green. Player text matches the game. Art goes through `CustomAssets` or `KenneyAssets` only. If architecture, Ascend, the world path, distribution, or tooling changed, update `AGENTS.md`.

## Phone, words, and git

Phones are about 360–430 px wide. The live look is the Samsung A56
(`a56-playtest`, 360×780). Web is a fallback, not the product. Testers
never get a build before the owner.

A whole screen or floor that changes size, speed, or layout gets a before
and an after on the A56. The owner picks. Small tweaks ship.

Say session (ett sittande), daily (dagens jobb), and run (ett varv). The
live hero is the cutout skeleton.

Talk in the owner's language, plain and short. In-game text stays English.
Do not explain tools unless they ask how.

When analyze and the matching tests are green, commit locally. A cloud or
local agent hands off on a branch and a PR. Do not merge unless the owner
asks. That push is not a `test-*` tag, a `v*` tag, or an APK workflow.
Never force-push or skip hooks unless they say so in that turn. Do not
stage `windows/flutter/generated_*` unless plugins changed. Split a giant
file instead of growing `game_logic`, `spatial_combat`, or a fat shell.
New HUD goes under `lib/ui/shell/`. Delete unused code that saves do not
need. Keep JSON fields old saves may still have.

Hand off in the owner's language: what you chose, why, what changed, and
what to try on a new save. End with 2–3 next ideas and one-line reasons
(at least one revenue). Do not start those ideas in this turn. Wait when
they should look at the phone, a whole screen or floor needs a
before-and-after, or a lock or missing fact blocks the next step.

## Workflow

Source work is a branch and a PR, in the cloud or locally. Do not put
ordinary agent work on `main`. Nothing merges unless the owner asks. A
test APK and a Play AAB stay where their workflows already are, and
neither starts unless the owner asks in that turn. Check the workflow
`on:` before a push. Priority is revenue.
